<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:27Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>As China's Communist Party holds plenum, Xi's anti-corruption drive continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73be6151060fed92c4f47cab29fe935afdaeb2e439b42f04ffee01c2e41f7607</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261027-as-china-s-communist-party-holds-plenum-xi-s-anti-corruption-drive-continues--b51be6c2b893.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261027-as-china-s-communist-party-holds-plenum-xi-s-anti-corruption-drive-continues" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, we try to figure out what happens behind the closed doors of the Chinese Communist Party's plenum meeting. At the heart of the discussions will be President Xi Jinping's firm grip on power. For analysis, we're joined by Jean-François Di Méglio from the Asia Centre think tank.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Azerbaijan: Rare protests over hijab ban in schools</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3957ff864d6a545a01c554f82dbc81eb850a4f3c22694a8fc0c8778fc4b3bd8</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:16:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools--72dbcc5dfced.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261027-azerbaijan-rare-protests-over-hijab-ban-in-schools" /><summary type="html">In Azerbaijan, a new government ban on hijab in schools has provoked rare public protests. The ban prohibits clothing deemed "incompatible with the secular principles of general education". While it does not mention Islamic hijab, girls and teachers wearing hijab have been turned away from schools. The measure has sparked tensions in a country where 96% of the population is Muslim.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Typhoon Champi batters Taiwan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1fbc97fee6bd22416e374dfd705ec4bf9e2437b443bcb8f95e95f456f4bcd942</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan--3f52c552700e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/typhoon-champi-batters-taiwan" /><summary type="html">Typhoon Champi is heading towards China and Japan. Yesterday, it battered Taiwan with heavy rain and winds reaching up to 180 kilometres per hour. Across the island, 56,000 households are without power. Nicolas Chamontin and Ophelie Jacobson report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why do women in public life become targets?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0a07abb33f86b7dba91c7a01228caf42422e71d0d35a6ebce00fd315b0e615</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:58:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets--350d0cae4873.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261023-why-do-women-in-public-life-become-targets" /><summary type="html">A brutal targeted attack on an Australian female MP, who lost both her legs as a result, has reignited concerns over the rising levels of violence against women in public life. Also Cornell University is facing a no-confidence vote over its handling of an alleged gang rape in 2024. Annette Young speaks to Annie E. Clark, a survivor of campus sexual assault and Dr Sara Wilf of George Mason University about why institutions continue to struggle with sexual assault cases.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Singapore's longevity industry: The quest for eternal youth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef07c3950021401f893669aff5fc3cdacad73974e354558a6a2e33b70fd8b4de</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth--7654b61f92cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth" /><summary type="html">In Singapore, the quest for eternal youth is no longer just a billionaire's fantasy. It's becoming big business. High-tech clinics, longevity labs and specialist companies all promise the same thing: slowing down the ageing process. From continuous metabolic monitoring and genetic testing to supplements and oxygen therapy, every aspect of the body is measured and optimised.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan shuts down schools and businesses as Typhoon Champi approaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23bd2a28bdfa77c74974527d2dbf34223fb014f01207c66c195ac3213994b24f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T03:00:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261023-taiwan-shuts-down-schools-and-businesses-as-typhoon-champi-approaches--0f72f77296ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261023-taiwan-shuts-down-schools-and-businesses-as-typhoon-champi-approaches" /><summary type="html">As Typhoon Champi approached Taiwan, most businesses and schools were closed across the island Friday and hundreds of flights were canceled in the region. Authorities reported at least one death and dozens of injuries and more than 1,200 people have evacuated their homes.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Strong earthquake strikes China’s remote Tibet region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:504b68486d2e350798c61f66973cf3845f96cf34743898e4956704628ec5182c</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T21:09:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261022-many-dead-massive-earthquake-strikes-china-s-remote-tibet-region-magnitude-seven--9ae8ceb17977.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261022-many-dead-massive-earthquake-strikes-china-s-remote-tibet-region-magnitude-seven" /><summary type="html">At least 16 people have died and dozens more injured after a major earthquake measuring 7.0 on the Richter scale shook China’s remote Tibet region on Thursday, state media said. Hundreds of houses collapsed in the tremor.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Dalai Lama appointed by China 'is going to be a fake one', exiled former Tibetan leader says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d6e6b426fd4d8c5484f089d5bf20c20ed8ce57dd3dc17473015e21f163b9a4c</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T10:22:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says--f8e9f1f22fcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, exiled former Tibetan leader Lobsang Sangay said any successor to the Dalai Lama appointed by China "is going to be a fake one". He also likened Beijing's ethnic unity law to "an ethnic erasure", said Tibetan concerns had been "downgraded a bit" in US-China talks and accused China of failing to warn of the deadly August floods on the Nepal-Tibet border.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia continues to battle wildfires, with nearly 2 million hectares burned</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff698cff3f6f9c579ab57e2570e925b8fd3e31350c21a93e41bbe23b22093016</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T10:23:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261020-indonesia-continues-to-battle-wildfires-with-nearly-2-million-hectares-burned--5514d17d6fb8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/down-to-earth/20261020-indonesia-continues-to-battle-wildfires-with-nearly-2-million-hectares-burned" /><summary type="html">Fires in Indonesia have burned through more than 1.9 million hectares of land, according to new data, as the country battles its worst wildfire season in a decade. The blazes have sent toxic smoke across much of Southeast Asia, forcing schools to close and fuelling a rise in respiratory illnesses. FRANCE 24's Environment Editor Valerie Dekimpe tells us more.</summary><category term="Down to Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Driver charged over 'targeted' car attack on Australian lawmaker Helen Haines</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20fdc5006676594d178166fb40d82c4ee77936791868d276dae8d5515b08357f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T02:39:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261020-driver-charged-over-targeted-car-attack-on-australian-lawmaker-helen-haines--a831b000d15c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261020-driver-charged-over-targeted-car-attack-on-australian-lawmaker-helen-haines" /><summary type="html">Police on Tuesday charged a driver with intentionally causing serious injury to Australian federal lawmaker Helen Haines, who is in a critical condition after being struck by a car outside her office in an incident that has shocked the nation. Haines had her leg amputated following the attack, according to Australian media reports.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Months-long Indonesia wildfires spew toxic haze across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c43a2d94c13f5b07af84f89d0c9ab95081f25810cd99ad6c448bcfdd5b0c3fd</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T06:30:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-months-long-indonesia-wildfires-spew-toxic-haze-across-southeast-asia--f065858c7f80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-months-long-indonesia-wildfires-spew-toxic-haze-across-southeast-asia" /><summary type="html">Parts of southern Southeast Asia have been put under the highest-level haze alert as wildfires that have swept Indonesia for months continue to belch toxic smoke across the region. The seasonal wildfires are worse this year due to the drought conditions caused by a severe "super-El Nino" effect.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>India's 'cockroach' movement founder released from police custody</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6798c465144c894f066991f6d9fba27069331fb480bb67c2376e06e435753d73</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T05:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-india-s-cockroach-movement-founder-released-from-police-custody--284536488984.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-india-s-cockroach-movement-founder-released-from-police-custody" /><summary type="html">Indian police released Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke from detention on Saturday after the activist was detained ahead of a rally calling for the resignation of India's chief election commissioner. Two other CJP leaders remain in custody after having been arrested while demonstrating at a protest site that police had ruled off-limits.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's forest fires spark public health crisis across Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddfe10bc4af9783f7f192bbf945e09f38c6fb35b11bc735bec4ec11305913f72</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:26:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261016-indonesia-s-forest-fires-spark-public-health-crisis-across-southeast-asia--ce92433485e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261016-indonesia-s-forest-fires-spark-public-health-crisis-across-southeast-asia" /><summary type="html">Massive wildfires in Indonesia show no sign of letting up. The environmental disaster is turning into a pollution crisis across Southeast Asia, as toxic haze from the blazes spread to neighbouring countries.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Indian authorities detain 'cockroach' movement founder Dipke ahead of new protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e43fec6473533c65426b2fb44d6f739e6dc07647db6555bef3593c613fafd888</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T06:39:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261016-indian-authorities-heighten-security-close-park-ahead-cockroach-movement-rally--7b06e6dcb92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261016-indian-authorities-heighten-security-close-park-ahead-cockroach-movement-rally" /><summary type="html">Indian authorities on Friday detained Abhijeet Dipke, the founder of the satirical youth movement "Cockroach Janta Party", ahead of a new protest in New Delhi, live images from the group showed. Police earlier closed a central New Delhi park in an attempt to stifle near-daily demonstrations calling for the election authority chief's resignation over the removal of more than 130 million people from voter lists.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan school roof collapse kills dozens of pupils, teacher in Peshawar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6d5e0aa906deb89b908610db369beea76eb4c9aa747fddb7122cd774e1c623d</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:02:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261015-pakistan-school-roof-collapse-kills-dozens-of-pupils-teacher-in-peshawar--9a905ed0517b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261015-pakistan-school-roof-collapse-kills-dozens-of-pupils-teacher-in-peshawar" /><summary type="html">A teacher and at least 32 pupils were killed when a school roof collapsed in the northwestern Pakistani city of Peshawar on Thursday, authorities said. At least twenty people were injured, three of them severely.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea test-fires submarine-launched cruise missiles amid rising tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8104b99040cdc8bd4014a757b4af81e660204cd51684f229fd7a77f20ac9966f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T23:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles--e31421af3b62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles" /><summary type="html">North Korea test-fired two types of submarine-launched strategic cruise missiles on Wednesday, state media KCNA reported Thursday, saying the launches posed no threat to neighbouring countries. The tests follow heightened tensions with South Korea after a September 21 landmine explosion in the Demilitarised Zone injured three South Korean soldiers.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>How far will 'Cockroach' movement go? India's youth-led protests defy Modi government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d9abb29c0ea1cba8675f86bb3fb25c9b3b303834517cf5f58fef245adbf569b</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T18:40:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government--26fd7d79299c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government" /><summary type="html">It all started as a bit of online satire by a few young people fed up by corruption. Clearly though, the "Cockroach" movement is no longer a laughing matter for India’s government, which has shut transport and blocked rallying points in the capital to quell the momentum of a youth-led mobilisation that's already brought down the education minister over rampant school exam cheating and is now spearheading the protests against the culling of names from voter rolls, with the electoral commission chief accused of bias.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>‘The idea that Modi must be feared because he holds all levers of power has gone out of the window’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20fd55295f0b8313406ef5dd799e99f0032b167c348bceab249312cdbfe9a947</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T16:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window--88dfae3f38b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window" /><summary type="html">Is Narendra Modi losing his most powerful political asset: the perception of invincibility? As India's youth protest movement confronts an increasingly combative government, Dr. Subir Sinha, Director of the SOAS South Asia Institute and Reader in Development Studies, argues that the political significance of the demonstrations extends far beyond the arrests of opposition activists and the growing confrontation between protesters and state institutions. Dr. Sinha examines how the government's increasingly repressive response may be exposing the fragility of its authority and institutional legitimacy. Could India's emerging protest movement be dismantling the political mythology that has sustained Modi's hold on power?</summary></entry><entry><title>Cheap weapons, growing fears: Inside the Taliban’s drone campaign against Pakistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2dcb0535763549365e800552b62d27790afcaa0bcaaefb4d05bf04fe5866533f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan--4d38ee0ab100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan" /><summary type="html">Pakistan says it intercepted 23 suicide drones launched from Afghanistan into Pakistani airspace in September alone. Since the conflict began in February 2026, the Taliban have increasingly used drones to attack Pakistan, raising concerns in Islamabad.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>‘Dark day for Turkey’: Police halt broadcasts, make arrests in raid on opposition TV</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a405b588b0d23559a12c9fc8b85730261db8390700b075c2d3d3c05d11daeb60</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:09:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-pro-opposition-tv-channel-boss-slams-police-raid-broadcast-halt--2027488a6f87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-pro-opposition-tv-channel-boss-slams-police-raid-broadcast-halt" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities appointed a government trustee to run popular broadcaster Halk TV on Wednesday after police raided its headquarters, halting live broadcasts and arresting 11 people. Halk chairman Cafer Mahirogluin denounced "a dark day for Turkey", adding that seven of his family members were among those detained.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Asia's fertility hub: Thailand emerges as top destination for IVF treatment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ca7f9cb0b03cfadbf69522005c25bbf1d59f3de0ac1b3bbc60a8e36a49ad91c</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T12:38:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261013-asia-s-fertility-hub-thailand-emerges-as-top-destination-for-ivf-treatment--bc3bbfd133c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261013-asia-s-fertility-hub-thailand-emerges-as-top-destination-for-ivf-treatment" /><summary type="html">Thailand has become one of Asia's leading fertility hubs. Every year, thousands of foreign patients travel to Bangkok's state-of-the-art private clinics for IVF, egg donation and other fertility treatments. They come from China, South Korea, Europe and across Southeast Asia, looking for what may be harder to find at home: shorter waiting times, lower costs and, in some cases, fewer restrictions.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>India’s youth-led Cockroach movement defies protest ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95bacd25a7581b348482d7df532b53353af75bd01dc4abb7ddfbc115ef7d606e</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:00:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-defies-protest-ban--510cf1269e48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-youth-led-cockroach-movement-defies-protest-ban" /><summary type="html">India’s youth-led Cockroach movement is intensifying protests against Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s government. Three leaders were detained after defying a ban at New Delhi’s Jantar Mantar protest site. Demonstrators are challenging a voter-list revision they claim favours Modi’s party, while the protests disrupt businesses across the capital.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands of Indians march to Supreme Court to oust election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:613c64395086f8477aca13995ca5d83cfd10c6be2aa2f8648bad87a73ce115c2</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T16:23:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief--cfcf565f6afb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-of-indians-march-to-supreme-court-to-oust-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Protesters in New Delhi continue to take to the streets demanding the country's top election commissioner resign. Frustrations have been mounting after an investigation in a leading newspaper revealed concerns had been raised within the body, over the revision of voter lists. Delano D'Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>India's opposition leader marches with thousands against election chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a052ce4ccd43973251cb1411e65ec713efe2269da308f3c93b8fc5d32dbb1ff2</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T15:14:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief--11dd429412fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/india-s-opposition-leader-marches-with-thousands-against-election-chief" /><summary type="html">Opposition parties and supporters of the so-called "cockroach" youth movement marched towards the country's Supreme Court on Monday, in the latest show of outrage against the recent removal of millions of names from voters lists. Critics say the move is likely to benefit Prime Minister Narendra Modi's ruling party – and are demanding India's election chief step down over what they describe as misconduct. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in New Delhi, Navodita Kumari.</summary></entry><entry><title>Five people missing as fresh flash floods hit central Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0258f5846cec6de3ab2ec99ee705e0b6710bc094d5febb0c8094b34df6aa4ed7</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:43:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal--2d9a2373d2a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-five-people-missing-as-fresh-flash-floods-hit-central-nepal" /><summary type="html">Nepali rescuers searched for five missing people on Monday, a day after new flash floods swept away more than 200 houses and five bridges along the Budhi Gandaki River. The country is still recovering from devastating floods, triggered by a mountain glacial collapse on August 26, which killed more than 1,400 people and left over 5,000 missing.</summary></entry><entry><title>Striking images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9eded444da874e3986c142f8c5815711ac258168a9f34a7280d9a4c83a44c66</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:14:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal--99e18aa6713c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/striking-images-show-new-flash-floods-hitting-central-nepal" /><summary type="html">Striking new images show new flash floods hitting central Nepal. This comes only six weeks after another disaster there left more than 1,400 dead and 5,000 missing. According to an initial assessment by the Nepalese authorities, at least five people are now missing. Elitsa Gadeva and France 2 have the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Illegal detentions' in India, as protesters allege foul play at Electoral Commission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e107adfc9b9081e18c39e68a24c6d4a1326ed58f162027f4da572767c82c38b</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:51:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261012-illegal-detentions-in-india-as-protesters-allege-foul-play-at-electoral-commission--04511ed70d4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261012-illegal-detentions-in-india-as-protesters-allege-foul-play-at-electoral-commission" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Monday, October 12: Widespread protests in India are met with detentions judged "illegal" by the country's Supreme Court. But first: Lebanese papers report as Hezbollah prepares for a new regional flare-up. Finally, Citroën hopes to win hearts and minds with an electric reboot of the vintage Deux Chevaux model.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Opposition leaders and journalists allege police abuses as fresh protests break out in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf54579575606c375a67d9e2684931161ec2360fc0d66d68ad6d56bc57e63d28</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T04:33:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-opposition-leaders-and-journalists-allege-police-abuses-as-fresh-protests-break-out-in-indi--008b7975f167.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-opposition-leaders-and-journalists-allege-police-abuses-as-fresh-protests-break-out-in-india" /><summary type="html">Indian opposition politicians and journalists alleged that police had been heavy-handed in cracking down in protests that swept New Delhi over the weekend in response to a nationwide voter roll revision that critics say disproportionately affects Muslim and other minority voters. Opposition leader Rahul Gandhi called for a fresh march to the nation's Supreme Court Monday.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Melbourne Islamic leader denies links to suspected FlyDubai hijacker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20a7bce2cacebe76e8757b2db22646603cd00fa41b9eca07db6a7d3c4189cb53</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T03:49:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-melbourne-man-linked-to-suspected-flydubai-hijacker-condemns-false-accusations--a41bc8875157.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-melbourne-man-linked-to-suspected-flydubai-hijacker-condemns-false-accusations" /><summary type="html">Abu Hamza, whose Melbourne-based Islamic community centre was linked by Emirati prosecutors to the suspect in the attempted hijacking of an Israel-bound passenger jet, publicly dismissed "false accusations" against him on Monday. While prosecutors alleged that the Omani co-pilot first became radicalised while studying in Australia, neither the community centre nor Hamza are accused of any criminal wrongdoing.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea fires multiple ballistic missiles off east coast, Seoul says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7da4b05f5d3aaee8c4aac7cf0ebbb2ba9a8c20073ba27021880d7a81e079b799</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T01:54:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-north-korea-ballistic-missiles-sea-japan-seoul--a82c58ea609e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261012-north-korea-ballistic-missiles-sea-japan-seoul" /><summary type="html">North Korea fired multiple ballistic missiles off its east coast on Monday, South Korea’s military said, amid tensions over border landmine explosions that injured three South Korean soldiers last month. Seoul said the missiles were launched from Pyongyang and increased surveillance, while Japan confirmed at least one suspected ballistic missile.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry></feed>
